# Legacy Jekyll project URLs -> current Astro URLs (301).
#
# The Jekyll site published projects as /projects/<NN>-<slug>(.html). The Astro
# site uses /projects/<slug>. nginx/default.conf normalizes the request path
# (drops .html and the trailing slash) before looking it up here, so each
# project needs only one line. Hits are logged to legacy-redirects.log; once
# that log stays empty for a few months this file can be deleted.
#
# Format: <old path> <new path>;

